  "version": "v2",
  "description": "High-recall exclusion gazetteer for the public tokenizer benchmark. A sentence matching any term is dropped before the 500-sentence Tanglish sample is frozen, so an inflammatory or political row cannot reach a public table. Latin exact terms match as whole words; Latin stems also accept a closed set of Tanglish case suffixes (pundaiku, mayirum, arasiyaluku); Tamil terms match at a word start with a known case suffix only (தேர்தலில், அமைச்சரை), which avoids சாதிக்க and புண்டரீகாட்சன்.",
  "native_review": "pending",
  "review_note": "v2 responds to review: inflected forms now match, over-broad terms (strike, war, government, inc, cpi, sunni) are removed, Tamil party names added, and Tamil matching is bounded so ordinary words no longer match by substring. A native reviewer must still extend and sign it off before the corpus is frozen for publication (see docs/EVAL_CORPUS.md). v2.1 adds named public figures that appear in the sample without party vocabulary (stalin, kanimozhi, seeman) and the abusive stem gaandu; short ambiguous abbreviations such as eps stay out because they matched 'Epstein'.",
